  ("Chemical Equilibrium: Le Chatelier's principle: a system at equilibrium shifts to oppose any change. Higher pressure favours the side with fewer gas moles; heating favours the endothermic direction; a catalyst changes the rate but not K.", "medium", "conceptual confusion"),
  ("Chemical Equilibrium: Reaction quotient Q: if Q < K the reaction goes forward, if Q > K it goes backward and if Q = K it is at equilibrium. K changes only with temperature.", "hard", "incorrect assumption"),
  ("Chemical Equilibrium: pH = -log[H+] and pOH = 14 - pH at 25 C. For a weak acid Ka = [H+][A-]/[HA] and alpha = sqrt(Ka/C) for small alpha. Buffer pH = pKa + log([salt]/[acid]).", "hard", "calculation error"),
